JWasm: -Zj gives a field's global symbol its SIZE and LENGTH

With -Zm, JWasm also defines each structure field as a global symbol, as
MASM 5 does, but without the size and length of its first initializer, so
SIZE and LENGTH of the bare name are those of its type.  In MASM 5, SIZE
FIELD of a DB 1024 DUP (?) field is 1024.  Under -Zj, the global symbol
gets the field's.

Needed for GRAFTABL's GRTAB.ASM, TABSIZE EQU SIZE LANCHAR + SIZE LANID +
SIZE LANNAME (0410h).

diff --git a/src/data.c b/src/data.c
index 1e22240..e5a6c32 100644
--- a/src/data.c
+++ b/src/data.c
@@ -1422,6 +1422,17 @@ ret_code data_dir( int i, struct asm_tok tokenarray[], struct asym *type_sym )
     /* v2.06: update struct size after ALL items have been processed */
     if ( CurrStruct )
         UpdateStructSize( sym );
+    /* -Zj: the global symbol of a field (-Zm) has its SIZE and LENGTH, as in
+     * Masm 5 (GRAFTABL's SIZE LANCHAR, a DB 1024 DUP (?) field) */
+    if ( CurrStruct && sym && Options.masm5_compat && ModuleInfo.oldstructs &&
+        Parse_Pass == PASS_1 && *sym->name ) {
+        struct asym *gsym = SymSearch( sym->name );
+        if ( gsym && gsym != sym && gsym->state == SYM_STRUCT_FIELD ) {
+            gsym->isdata = TRUE;
+            gsym->first_size = sym->first_size;
+            gsym->first_length = sym->first_length;
+        }
+    }
 
     if ( ModuleInfo.list )
         //LstWrite( CurrStruct ? LSTTYPE_STRUCT : LSTTYPE_DATA, currofs, sym ); /* v2.18: sym not used by LSTTYPE _STRUCT/_DATA */
